\par\par \b \uc2  ODJ BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  More To Slow Yen Rally Than Reverse It \b0\par\par\uc2 1,002 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 21:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones Commodities Service \par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -- Repeating story from earlier\par    By Grainne McCarthy\par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- After finally showing its hand and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now faces the tough task of following through\par in its\par effort to weaken the yen, fighting a tide of sentiment that seems\par determined to\par push the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stronger.\par   But U.S.-based analysts argue that Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par cognizant\par of this and - in a break from previous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - is acting this\par time more\par to slow the pace of the yen's rise than to actively weaken it."It's a\par smoothing\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said David Gilmore, partner at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analytics\par in Essex,\par Conn.\par   "They know investors globally are underweight Japan, they also are\par aware that\par their economy is improving and they're recognizing that the rest of the\par world\par is starting to believe that story as well," he added.\par   Indeed, despite the plethora of structural problems at the heart of\par Japan's\par economy, the country is showing signs of a cyclical recovery. Against\par news that\par industrial production rose in March for the second straight month and\par as\par analysts up their forecast for growth in first quarter gross domestic\par to above\par 6%, fund managers are pouring funds into Japanese stocks. The Bank of\par Japan\par Wednesday upgraded its economic assessment for the third consecutive\par month\par saying the economy was worsening at a slower rate, citing, among other\par things,\par rebounding exports.\par   Against this backdrop, the yen has rallied almost relentlessly,\par jumping about\par 6% in the past month and over 2% this week alone. The Japanese unit has\par also\par been pushed along by a swell of negative momentum towards the dollar,\par which is\par under pressure from heightened terrorism concerns, a struggling stock\par market, a\par burgeoning current account deficit and a bid by global investors to\par seek\par higher-yielding returns elsewhere.\par   In this sense, spending billions of dollars now in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market to weaken the yen could amount to a wasted effort. "The fact\par that\par they're fighting broader dollar weakness makes the battle that much\par tougher,"\par said Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast financial consultancy in\par New York.\par "What they have to do is not just turn around yen strength, but the\par strength of\par the other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well. If they're all pointed to a weaker\par dollar, they\par will pull the yen with them."\par     Making Good On Rounds Of Jawboning\par   After repeated verbal attempts to talk the rallying yen down, Japan's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  finally put its money where its mouth is in Tokyo\par trading\par Wednesday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the dollar had\par tumbled\par to a seven-month low of Y123.51 earlier in the day.\par   The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which took place at levels close to  Y123.70,\par hoisted the\par greenback a full yen, sending a strong message to the market in the\par process\par that Tokyo is serious about taming the rampaging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The effect\par proved\par relatively short-lived, however: in early afternoon New York trade\par Wednesday,\par the dollar was almost as weak as late Tuesday in New York, changing\par hands at\par around Y124.21.\par   But analysts believe that given the slew of positive factors\par supporting the\par yen now, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did reap some measure of success in that it\par slowed\par the ferocity of the yen's climb. "They're clearly sensitive to recent\par moves,"\par said Allison Montgomery, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Morgan Stanley, in\par New York.\par "Our view is that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains defensive, rather than\par offensive."\par   If this is indeed the aim of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , there's every reason\par to\par believe it will continue if the dollar falls rapidly again, as it did\par during\par Tuesday's global day when the greenback fell by over two yen. Japanese\par policy\par makers have repeatedly stated their desire for a more stable exchange\par rate and\par routinely express their concern after rapid price moves.\par   "Speed is going to be important in terms of the BOJ coming in again,\par as well\par as what's happening with other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Ruskin. If, for\par instance, the\par dollar is weak across the board at the same time that it's weak against\par the\par yen, "that's a good indication that it's a dollar-led rather than\par yen-led\par move."\par   Indeed, part of the reason why the finance ministry - the guardian of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy - ordered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now was a sense that\par Tuesday's sharp jump in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  represented a shift in market\par sentiment\par away from a yen rallying simply because the dollar is weak, towards an\par independent yen strength story.\par     Not A Speculator's Party\par   What's more, major banks report that fund flow indicators show that\par longer-term investors are buying into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovery story.\par Traditionally,\par the BOJ is more reluctant to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the market action is\par dominated by\par short-term speculators.\par   If the Japanese authorities are serious about defending the dollar -\par which is\par now broadly weak - they would have to spend amounts on the scale of the\par last\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the Sept. 11 attacks, when the government forked out\par an\par estimated $2.3 trillion worth of yen in ten rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The\par major\par difference now, however, is that the outlook for the Japanese economy\par looks\par much more promising than it did back then.\par   The market will also be looking to see if the BOJ will buy back the\par extra yen\par it sold to the market, or leave the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unsterilized by\par allowing the\par increased amount of yen in circulation to simply boost the money\par supply.\par   If it decides to mop up the extra funds, "the market will continue to\par sell\par the dollar while it stays weak globally," says Mansoor Mohi-uddin,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore. "In this respect, (Wednesday's)\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would then be similar to (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's) fruitless\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par 1999 when the dollar continued to fall sharply."\par   -Grainne McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4156;\par grainne.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1936GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djcs000020020522dy5m00qus\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
