\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  More To Slow Yen Rally Than Reverse It \b0\par\par\uc2  By Grainne McCarthy \par \uc2 1,072 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 20:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- After finally showing its hand and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  now faces the tough task of following through in its effort to weaken the yen, fighting a tide of sentiment that seems determined to push the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger. \par \par \uc2  But U.S.-based analysts argue that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is cognizant of this and - in a break from previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - is acting this time more to slow the pace of the yen's rise than to actively weaken it."It's a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Conn. \par \par \uc2  "They know investors globally are underweight Japan, they also are aware that their economy is improving and they're recognizing that the rest of the world is starting to believe that story as well," he added. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, despite the plethora of structural problems at the heart of Japan's economy, the country is showing signs of a cyclical recovery. Against news that industrial production rose in March for the second straight month and as analysts up their forecast for growth in first quarter gross domestic to above 6%, fund managers are pouring funds into Japanese stocks. The Bank of Japan Wednesday upgraded its economic assessment for the third consecutive month saying the economy was worsening at a slower rate, citing, among other things, rebounding exports. \par \par \uc2  Against this backdrop, the yen has rallied almost relentlessly, jumping about 6% in the past month and over 2% this week alone. The Japanese unit has also been pushed along by a swell of negative momentum towards the dollar, which is under pressure from heightened terrorism concerns, a struggling stock market, a burgeoning current account deficit and a bid by global investors to seek higher-yielding returns elsewhere. \par \par \uc2  In this sense, spending billions of dollars now in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the yen could amount to a wasted effort. "The fact that they're fighting broader dollar weakness makes the battle that much tougher," said Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast financial consultancy in New York. "What they have to do is not just turn around yen strength, but the strength of the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well. If they're all pointed to a weaker dollar, they will pull the yen with them." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Making Good On Rounds Of Jawboning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After repeated verbal attempts to talk the rallying yen down, Japan's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  finally put its money where its mouth is in Tokyo\par trading Wednesday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the\par dollar had tumbled to a seven-month low of Y123.51 earlier in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which took place at levels close to  Y123.70,\par hoisted the greenback a full yen, sending a strong message to the market\par in the process that Tokyo is serious about taming the rampaging\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The effect proved relatively short-lived, however: in early\par afternoon New York trade Wednesday, the dollar was almost as weak as\par late Tuesday in New York, changing hands at around Y124.21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But analysts believe that given the slew of positive factors\par supporting the yen now, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did reap some measure of\par success in that it slowed the ferocity of the yen's climb. "They're\par clearly sensitive to recent moves," said Allison Montgomery, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at Morgan Stanley, in New York. "Our view is that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains defensive, rather than offensive."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If this is indeed the aim of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , there's every reason to\par believe it will continue if the dollar falls rapidly again, as it did\par during Tuesday's global day when the greenback fell by over two yen.\par Japanese policy makers have repeatedly stated their desire for a more\par stable exchange rate and routinely express their concern after rapid\par price moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Speed is going to be important in terms of the BOJ coming in again,\par as well as what's happening with other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Ruskin. If, for\par instance, the dollar is weak across the board at the same time that it's\par weak against the yen, "that's a good indication that it's a dollar-led\par rather than yen-led move."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indeed, part of the reason why the finance ministry - the guardian of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy - ordered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now was a\par sense that Tuesday's sharp jump in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  represented a shift in\par market sentiment away from a yen rallying simply because the dollar is\par weak, towards an independent yen strength story.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Not A Speculator's Party\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par What's more, major banks report that fund flow indicators show that\par longer-term investors are buying into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovery story.\par Traditionally, the BOJ is more reluctant to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the market\par action is dominated by short-term speculators.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the Japanese authorities are serious about defending the dollar -\par which is now broadly weak - they would have to spend amounts on the\par scale of the last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the Sept. 11 attacks, when the\par government forked out an estimated $2.3 trillion worth of yen in ten\par rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The major difference now, however, is that the\par outlook for the Japanese economy looks much more promising than it did\par back then.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market will also be looking to see if the BOJ will buy back the\par extra yen it sold to the market, or leave the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unsterilized\par by allowing the increased amount of yen in circulation to simply boost\par the money supply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If it decides to mop up the extra funds, "the market will continue to\par sell the dollar while it stays weak globally," says Mansoor Mohi-uddin,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore. "In this respect,\par (Wednesday's) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would then be similar to (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's) fruitless\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 1999 when the dollar continued to fall sharply."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Grainne McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4156;\par grainne.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the Japanese authorities are serious about defending the dollar -\par which is broadly weak - they would have to spend amounts on the scale of\par the last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the Sept. 11 attacks, when the government\par forked out an estimated $23 billion worth of yen in 10 rounds of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (In an item that moved at around 2:18 p.m. EDT (1818 GMT), the amount\par spent by the BOJ in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after Sept. 11 was misstated).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020522dy5m008y9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
