\par\par \b \uc2  Runaway gold sets new safe-haven high in early NY. \b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 16:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 22 (Reuters) - COMEX gold set a new high for the year early Wednesday near $320 an ounce on jitters about the hair-trigger tensions between India and Pakistan and the threat of another terror attack on New York landmarks. \par \par \uc2  Gold has turned from a dog into the darling of the investment world in 2002, using the bullish groundwork laid in last year's U.S. recession, interest rate cuts, and the Sept. 11 terror attacks to turn the corner on two-decade bear market, according to analysts. \par \par \uc2  "With the stock markets in the USA continuing their vicious declines, with the vice-president of the USA warning its populace of imminent terrorist activities, with continuing fears in regards to the escalation of violence in both the Middle East and India/Pakistan, and the dollar somewhat in question, the gold market remains amazingly strong," Leonard Kaplan, president of Prospector Asset Management, wrote in a client report Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the sixth straight day of safe-haven buying, June gold at 0914 EDT was up $1.70 at $317.80 an ounce, after moving from $315.60 to $319.80 in overnight Access trade, its highest since June 2000, when the contract was thinly traded toward the back of the board. \par \par \uc2  "People are definitely jittery and taking a wait-and-see attitude," said a trader at a bullion trading firm. "At this level I don't think anyone is aggressive (enough) to initiate positions. Possibly all the short covering has been done and longs are hanging in there." \par \par \uc2  Spot gold was quoted at $317.90/8.40, up from the close at $315.80/6.30 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Gold fixed early Wednesday at $318.25 an ounce, and topped at $319.60 its highest price since the massive spike to $338 in October 1999 on the back of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement to limit sales and dispel the worry that pushed bullion to a 20-year low in August of that year. \par \par \uc2  Gold's traditional role as a sanctuary reasserted itself Wednesday after India's Prime Minister Atal Behari Vajpayee told Indian soldiers confronting Pakistani forces across their border that the time had come for a decisive fight. \par \par \uc2  The neighbors, both nuclear powers, have amassed more than a million troops along the border since India blamed a deadly December attack on its parliament on Pakistan-backed Islamic militants. \par \par \uc2  The armies have exchanged heavy fire for six days running after another murderous assault last week on an Indian army camp by suspected Pakistan-based Kashmiri separatists. \par \par \uc2  London gold traders were jarred by news that Britain was set to withdraw some of its embassy staff from Pakistan in response to security threats. \par \par \uc2  In New York, the temporary closure of the Brooklyn Bridge after the discovery of a suspicious package, later found not to be a bomb, also unnerved traders. \par \par \uc2  Federal law enforcement officials also reported vague threats against the Statue of Liberty and the city imposed the toughest security measures since just after the World Trade Center was destroyed by suicide hijackers 8-1/2 months ago. \par \par \uc2  A major factor in the rise of gold, which was traditionally seen as a form of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is this week's dollar fall, which makes bullion cheaper for investors outside the United States. \par \par \uc2  The greenback hit a 27-month low Wednesday against the Swiss franc, another popular safe-haven. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen, which rose to a five-month high against the dollar, while the euro rose to a 15-month high. \par \par \uc2  "Its the news. It's short covering. All that stuff is in the market," said a COMEX gold broker. \par \par \uc2  July silver was off 5.5 cents at $4.79 an ounce, correcting after soaring Tuesday to a 15-month high at $4.865. The range so far was $4.86 to $4.78. \par \par \uc2  Spot silver fetched $4.79/81, down from $4.82/84 late Tuesday and Wednesday's fix at $4.82. \par \par \uc2  NYMEX July platinum was up $2 at $540 an ounce. Spot platinum was quoted at $542/549. \par \par \uc2  Illiquid June palladium was off another $12.15 at $358 an ounce, extending Tuesday's $12.65 shakeout. Spot palladium fetched $352/367. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020522dy5m00ojh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
