\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar edges off post- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  highs vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 14:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 22 (Reuters) - The dollar pared gains against the yen in European trading hours on Wednesday, edging back towards levels at which Japan earlier sold its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's export-damaging strength. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar moved clear of 28-month lows against the Swiss franc and eight-month lows against the euro, after New York's Brooklyn Bridge reopened following a security alert. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has shown broad weakness in recent weeks on concern over the performance of U.S. assets and on the relative pace of a U.S. economic recovery. Worries about further attacks on U.S. soil following the suicide attacks of September 11 have also reduced the appeal of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are in a new softer dollar environment. We have generalised broad dollar weakness," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One. \par \par \uc2  "It's very difficult for a \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take on the rest of the market and the BOJ will have to come in again." \par \par \uc2  The greenback shot up after the Bank of Japan was seen buying dollars on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in Tokyo trade from around 123.80 yen and above. Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa confirmed there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa first hinted \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen down, but later said he had not given such instructions. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo is worried that a stronger yen would hurt exporters and damage the country's fragile economic recovery. The Bank of Japan upgraded its view of the economy for a third straight month on Wednesday and Tokyo stocks rose to nine-month highs. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 124.41/45 yen at 1145 GMT, up less than a quarter percent from the U.S. close and well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  high of 125.08. The dollar hit a 5-1/2 month low of around 123.50 yen on Wednesday prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market's just trying to see if they're (Japanese authorities) still about but I can't see them letting it collapse," said a trader from a UK bank. \par \par \uc2  EURO LEAPS \par \par \uc2  The euro made more dramatic gains against the yen, benefiting doubly from broad dollar weakness and from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap yen strength. \par \par \uc2  It was trading at 115.23/26 yen, up one percent on the day and nearly two yen above two-month lows set before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading against the dollar at $0.9250/60 from highs of $0.9275, which were only around half a cent below levels last seen in the aftermath of September 11. The dollar was at 1.5688/91 Swiss francs from lows of 1.5660. \par \par \uc2  The FBI warned New York late on Tuesday about threats to city landmarks including the Brooklyn Bridge and the Statue of Liberty. The dollar suffered against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the safe haven Swiss franc, after the Bridge closed for about an hour before reopening around 1005 GMT with police reporting no major problem. \par \par \uc2  "If U.S. authorities are going to be continually reminding us about attacks, it can only undermine confidence in investing in the U.S.," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  Conflict between India and Pakistan was also benefiting the Swiss franc. Indian Prime Minister Atal Behari Vajpayee told Indian solders confronting Pakistani forces across their border in disputed Kashmir that the time had come for a decisive fight. \par \par \uc2  Swiss authorities are concerned about their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid rise. On Wednesday, the Swiss National Bank shaved its repo rate by two basis points to 1.03 percent because of the franc's strength. \par \par \uc2  BOJ ACTION \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably carried out via specific banks with which the bank has a relationship, rather than via electronic broking services. \par \par \uc2  "They have come in several times, doing small amounts," said a trader from a Japanese bank, estimating the total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount as much as $4-$5 billion. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda said in European trading hours that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some London traders said there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the European session, possibly via Japanese trust banks. \par \par \uc2  Markets had been put on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert on Tuesday as the dollar crashed through option barriers at 125 yen after a host of Japanese policymakers, including the Prime Minister, complained about the yen strength. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020522dy5m00k7t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
