\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , U.S. attack fears pull at dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 877 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 12:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 22 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped more than one yen from a five-month low on Wednesday after Japan sold the yen to cap its export-harming strength, but the dollar fell against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on fears of attacks on the United States. \par \par \uc2  The greenback shot up after the Bank of Japan was seen buying dollars on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  from around 123.80 yen and above. Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa confirmed the action. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar fell to eight-month lows against the euro and 28-month lows against the Swiss franc, adding to recent losses on concerns about U.S. assets and the pace of the U.S. recovery, after New York's Brooklyn Bridge was closed when a "suspicious package" was found there. It later reopened. \par \par \uc2  "We are in a new softer dollar environment. We have generalised broad dollar weakness," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One. \par \par \uc2  "It's very difficult for a \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take on the rest of the market, and the BOJ will have to come in again." \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa later sent mixed signals, first hinting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen down, but then saying he had not given such instructons. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo is worried that a stronger yen would hurt exporters and damage the country's fragile economic recovery. The Bank of Japan upgraded its view of the economy for a third straight month on Wednesday, and Tokyo stocks rose to nine-month highs. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 124.58/60 at 1012 GMT, up a third of a percent on the day but below earlier highs of 125.08. \par \par \uc2  EURO IN FASHION \par \par \uc2  The euro made more dramatic gains against the yen, benefiting doubly from broad dollar weakness and from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap yen strength. \par \par \uc2  It was trading near the day's highs at 115.42/47, a rise of 1.3 percent from the U.S. close and two yen above two-month lows set before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro also rose by 0.75 percent on the day to eight-month highs of $0.9275, around half a cent below levels last seen in the aftermath of September 11. The dollar fell by 0.70 percent to 28-month lows against the safe haven Swiss franc of 1.5660. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone's selling the dollar, they're buying the franc, they're buying euros as we're hearing the Brooklyn Bridge is shut. The situation between India and Pakistan is not too helpful either, they've both got the bomb," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The FBI warned New York late on Tuesday about threats to city landmarks including the Brooklyn Bridge and the Statue of Liberty. The Bridge closed for about an hour before reopening around 1005 GMT with police reporting no major problem. \par \par \uc2  Indian Prime Minister Atal Behari Vajpayee told Indian solders confronting Pakistani forces across their border in disputed Kashmir that the time had come for a decisive fight. \par \par \uc2  The British government confirmed it was pulling some nationals out of Pakistan after a "terrorist threat". \par \par \uc2  SMALL FRY \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably carried out via specific banks with which the bank has a relationship, rather than via electronic broking services. \par \par \uc2  They estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent between $1.0 and $3.0 billion in forcing the yen down, a drop in the ocean of the $1.2 trillion daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but enough to send a warning to the market. \par \par \uc2  "If they don't come in again, the dollar will go lower," said a trader from a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said in European trading hours that a move of five or more yen in a week was problematic - the yen has rallied from levels beyond 128 per dollar a week ago. \par \par \uc2  He also said he had no intention of asking for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the United States. Analysts and dealers have questioned the U.S. commitment to its strong dollar policy in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda said in European trading hours that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but London traders said it was unclear if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place during the European session. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been rising in recent weeks as the outlook for Japan's long-suffering economy improves and share prices there are seen offering better value at a time when investors are questioning the relative attraction of U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  Markets had been put on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert on Tuesday as the dollar crashed through option barriers at 125 yen after a host of Japanese policymakers including even the Prime Minister complained about the yen strength. \par \par \uc2  "It's going to be impossible for Japan to keep the yen down. They can only moderate its rise, not reverse it," said Rob Hayward, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN-Amro. \par \par \uc2  "The underlying flows still favour Japan. They're going to have to continue the action." \par \par \uc2  Swiss authorities are also concerned about their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the Swiss National Bank shaved its repo rate by two basis points to 1.03 percent because of the franc's strength. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020522dy5m00hlh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
