\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Shiokawa sends mixed message on future  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  steps. \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 22 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa sent mixed signals on Wednesday on future action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, first hinting of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise but later saying he hadn't given such instructions. \par \par \uc2  "I haven't given any instruction at all," Shiokawa told a news conference when asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would follow up on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa earlier confirmed the MOF had taken "appropriate action" in the market and he told Reuters it would probably continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen's rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa told the news conference \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no intention of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the United States and Europe. \par \par \uc2  The yen was quoted at 124.66 to the dollar at 0920 GMT. It briefly rose to 123.50, its highest level in five and a half months, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it back to around 125 yen. \par \par \uc2  STILL VIGILANT \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa made it clear, however, that rapid movements in the yen's exchange rate presented a problem. \par \par \uc2  "It's problematic for everyone when the yen moves rapidly, by five, seven yen in one week," he told the news conference. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's right-hand man and the country's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, reiterated that the ministry would stay vigilant. \par \par \uc2  "We have continued to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kuroda told Reuters. "We will continue to monitor the market with vigilance." \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders had described the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier as intermittent buying of dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes Japanese exports more expensive and deflates the yen value of income earned abroad. \par \par \uc2  Many economists believe that recovery prospects for the world's second-largest economy, currently mired in its worst downtrend in decades, depends almost solely on exports. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan upgraded its economic assessment on Wednesday for a third straight month, citing improvements in exports as well as inventories and industrial output. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020522dy5m00f5e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
