\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr jumps from 5-month low on yen after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 22 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a five-month low against the yen on Wednesday then jumped in mid-afternoon Tokyo trade after the Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the greenback for the first time since September. \par \par \uc2  The dollar quickly rose above 125 yen after the Bank of Japan (BOJ), acting as agent for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was seen buying dollars at 123.80-123.90 yen. \par \par \uc2  By 0630 GMT it was quoted around 124.70/74 yen in choppy trade after hitting a high of 125.10. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  "took appropriate action" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and would continue to monitor rates closely, responding as needed. \par \par \uc2  "Recent movements of the exchange rate have been too rapid. We have taken appropriate action today in the exchange market," he said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities have complained repeatedly about the yen's rise against the dollar, worried that it would choke off a nascent recovery in the economy which has been largely export-led. \par \par \uc2  The brighter prospects for Japan's economy and a resulting rise in Japanese share prices were cited by dealers as factors behind the yen's rise, leaving the dollar some four percent down on the week when it dropped to a 5-= month low of 123.50 yen in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar jumped suddenly by about one yen from around 123.80-123.90 yen after the BOJ was detected stepping in," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Since the dollar was sold aggressively in offshore trade yesterday, the market wants to see whether the BOJ will continue its efforts during overseas trading hours," he added. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was said to be buying dollars intermittently around 125 yen, with some traders saying the scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed relatively large. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 115.04/09 yen after dropping to a fresh two-month low of around 113.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR STILL BEARISH \par \par \uc2  The dollar regained some strength against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had risen to a multi-month highs earlier in the day before the BOJ's action. \par \par \uc2  However, underlying sentiment for the dollar was still bearish amid growing worries about further possible attacks on the United States. \par \par \uc2  "Fund operators and speculators are still eagerly trying to drive down the dollar and there are plenty of dollar-selling factors out there," a senior trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is reluctant to buy dollars when the U.S. government is saying they are expecting attacks. And investors are reluctant to hold U.S. assets heavily when we saw both the stock and bond markets being closed after the September attacks," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9211/15 after advancing earlier to a seven-month high of around $0.9244. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc backed off slightly to 1.5750/57 against the dollar after rising to an eight-month high at 1.5695 francs in the afternoon session. \par \par \uc2  The FBI has warned about threats to New York landmarks including the Statue of Liberty. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was undermined by a warning on Sunday from U.S. Vice President Dick Cheney that new attacks in the United States were "almost certain". \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0638 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   21 May. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9213   0.9200   +0.14    -2.98   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen        124.67   124.11   +0.45    +8.93   114.45\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    114.84   113.95   +0.78    +5.64   108.71\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.5750   1.5774   -0.15    -1.64   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr        1.4586   1.4597   -0.08    -2.76   1.5000\par  Can/dlr        1.5373   1.5364   +0.06    +3.08   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr        0.5575   0.5564   +0.20    -0.34   0.5594\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4513   1.4507   +0.04    -4.65   1.5221\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg    0.6314   0.6300   +0.22    -0.17   0.6325\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ..  Debt... Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Official rates...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......   Top events........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Diaries........... Diaries Index........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press Digests....  Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 D