\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar rises above 125 yen after BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 124 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 08:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 22 (Reuters) - The dollar rose above 125 yen on Wednesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the ailing greenback, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar fell to a new five-and-a-half-month low of 123.50 yen, but after the BOJ's dollar buying it rose as high as 125.02 yen in mid-afternoon Tokyo trading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  After the BOJ's move, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said his ministry had taken appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has exclusive authority for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020522dy5m007qc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
