\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar recoup losses as Shiokawa sounds serious. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2002\par 04:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 21 (Reuters) - The dollar bounced back on Tuesday from a five-month low against the yen after Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa made some tougher comments expressing his concern about the yen's recent strength. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa, describing recent market moves as unnatural, said his ministry would have to respond to any market manipulation. \par \par \uc2  "The recent volatility makes me sense something other than market principle is at work," he told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  The comments marked Shiokawa's first flat warning against the yen's strength in recent months, although Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko Kuroda and some other ministry officials have been saying the ministry would act in the market if necessary. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the ministry's top two spokesman on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kuroda and Zembei Mizoguchi, the head of the ministry's international bureau, also restated that the ministry was prepared to take appropriate actions in the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar recovered to 126.07 yen , compared with 125.35 in late New York trade and was nearly a full yen higher than its five-month low of 125.18 hit in New York. \par \par \uc2  As of 0222, it was bid at 125.88. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise against the yen also helped the greenback gain some ground against the euro. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped to 91.73 cents , from 92.11 in late U.S. trade and its seven-month peak around 92.30 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro firmed slightly to 115.65 , compared with 115.43 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  UNCONVINCED OF DOLLAR'S STRENGTH \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's hefty gains on Tuesday morning, most dealers were still expecting worries about the U.S. asset market to continue to nag the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near future. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. asset market is getting less attractive, especially relative to other markets. There's no doubt about that," said Hidehiko Inamura, vice president at Citibank N.A. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said that after years of ignoring the massive U.S. trade imbalance, the market was now paying increasing attention to the deficit, which tends to weaken a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have provided no less than 40 percent of new U.S. capital in the past six years, according to the Federal Reserve. That cash has helped fund the current account deficit, which runs at about four percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Vice President Dick Cheney on Sunday that another attack on the United States was "almost certain" also spooked a market that already has a diminished appetite for U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a global recovery are also encouraging investors to re-allocate funds from U.S. to other markets, including Japan. \par \par \uc2  Japan's main Nikkei share average fell slightly on Tuesday but is close to this year's peak of a little above 12,034.04. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers are still betting the dollar will fall in the near term, which will test the resolve of Japanese authorities to stop its fall. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely at this stage because it would be difficult for Japan to use the poor state of the economy as an excuse to weaken the yen since the government last week upgraded its official economic assessment. \par \par \uc2  "Share prices are considered to be a good indicator of how people are viewing the economy. So unless the Nikkei share average drops below 10,000, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to step in," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Others said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the dollar if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls below 120 yen, which would stifle yen-based profits of Japanese exporters. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0225 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 20 May.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9175   0.9211   -0.39    +3.04   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen               125.82   125.35   +0.37    -4.41   131.63\par  Euro/yen              115.56   115.43   +0.11    -1.43   117.24\par  Dlr/swiss             1.5832   1.5764   +0.43    -4.59   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr               1.4563   1.4580   -0.12    +0.15   1.4541\par  Can/dlr               1.5427   1.5414   +0.08    -3.08   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr               0.5537   0.5555   -0.32    +8.44   0.5106\par  Euro/swiss            1.4530   1.4528   +0.01    -1.69   1.4780\par  Euro/stg              0.6293   0.6315   -0.35    +2.78   0.6123.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020521dy5l0040l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
