\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen sprints to year's highs against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2002\par 14:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 17 (Reuters) - The yen soared by 1.5 percent to its highest levels this year against the dollar on Friday after comments from a Japanese official reduced wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  Masahiro Kawai, deputy Vice Minister for Intenational Finance at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told a conference in London that the Japanese government and the Bank of Japan rejected the idea of artifically driving the yen lower. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda later told Reuters Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy had not changed. But analysts and dealers said Kuroda's remarks had had limited impact, as the initial comments caught traders short of yen ahead of U.S. trade data at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The comment from the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  caught the market offguard and pushed the yen higher," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  "There is also bearish dollar sentiment ahead of the trade data." \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities are thought to be uncomfortable with the recently firming yen, preferring relative weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to stimulate exports and domestic growth. \par \par \uc2  The dollar lost nearly two yen on the day to a low of 126.19, its poorest showing since December 14, before recovering to 126.55/61 by 1200 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still there," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  "The further down the dollar goes, the higher the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  DATA ALERT \par \par \uc2  The U.S. March trade deficit is expected to swell slightly to $31.79 billion in March from $31.51 billion the previous month, a further negative for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. needs to suck in foreign capital inflows worth over $1.0 billion a day to plug its current account deficit, and recent signs of reduced overseas appetite for U.S. assets have hit the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "One of the causes of this dollar-negative sentiment is concern about current account funding," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "A widening of the deficit beyond the consensus forecast would be a signal to sell the dollar, and the market loves to find reasons to sell the dollar at the moment." \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, Japan's current account surplus, figures for which were released on Wednesday, rose 51.8 percent to 2.2 trillion yen ($17.18 billion) in March, with the trade surplus gaining 27.5 percent to 1.41 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government officially declared the economy was past its worst in its May economic assessment, upgrading its view of conditions for a third month. \par \par \uc2  Also on the U.S. data slate is the University of Michigan's preliminary consumer sentiment index for May at 1345 GMT, forecast to come in at 92.7 compared with the previous 93. \par \par \uc2  The euro avoided the volatility of the dollar/yen exchange rate, trading at $0.9139/44, a gain of a third of a percent against the broadly weaker dollar. \par \par \uc2  STERLING REELS \par \par \uc2  Sterling hit the year's lows against the euro of 62.87 pence on mounting speculation the British government is eyeing a referendum on joining the euro. \par \par \uc2  British Transport Secretary Stephen Byers, in what he thought was an off-the-record aside to journalists, suggested on Thursday that the government could include a bill setting up the technical structure for a euro referendum in its legislative programme for the next parliamentary session which begins in November. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Tony Blair's official spokesman dismissed the idea, but speculation remained after Blair gave his strongest endorsement of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to date this week in a BBC television interview. \par \par \uc2  "The heat in the EMU debate has been turned up a bit this week, first with Blair's pro-EMU comments and now Byers," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax. \par \par \uc2  Sterling needs to weaken against the euro before it can join monetary union in order to maintain Britain's competitiveness, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Swiss franc was steady against the euro after the Swiss National Bank shaved two basis points of its repo rates to 1.05 percent, in what traders said was a continued effort to stem a recent export-harming rally in the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020517dy5h00o2q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
