\par\par \b \uc2  Yen dips back slightly after Kuroda comment on yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2002\par 13:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 17 (Reuters) - The yen dipped back a little from five month highs struck against the dollar on Friday after Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda said Japan would take action if needed on the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities are thought to be uncomfortable with a firming yen, preferring relative weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in orer to stimulate exports and domestic growth. \par \par \uc2  However, the yen surged after comments made by a Japanese finance ministry official in London who said Japan had no intention of articifially weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Kuroda's comments were taken in the market as a swift rebuttal of any notion that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy may have changed. \par \par \uc2  "The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still there," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers, adding that the weaker the yen got the greater the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Masahiro Kawai, deputy Vice Minister for Intenational Finance at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had told a conference organised by ratings agency Fitch in London: \par \par \uc2  "They (the government and the BoJ) clearly reject the idea of resorting to a beggar-thy-neighbour \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy of driving the yen artificially lower." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the comments were a surprise and had had a clear impact in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The comment from the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  caught the market off guard and pushed the yen higher," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  At 1145 GMT, the yen was quoted at 126.48 to the dollar, having been as firm as 126.19 prior to Kuroda's comments. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020517dy5h00n6a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
