\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  reserves at record high, no Q1  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2002\par 03:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official reserves swelled to a record high in April as gains in massive U.S. Treasury holdings added to the world's largest stockpile of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The reserves - a key measure of a country's ability to meet its foreign obligations - have more than doubled since 1995 as Japan bought dollars to prevent the yen from strengthening and used the funds to purchase U.S. bonds. \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted no \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the January-March quarter, reserves still rose to $406.700 billion at the end of April, topping a record high posted in October. \par \par \uc2  "The rise was due to gains in securities holdings," a ministry official told reporters. \par \par \uc2  About 70 percent of Japan's reserves are believed to be held in the form of U.S. Treasuries, which rallied in April on the Federal Reserve's uncertain view of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  Japan has long boasted the biggest reserves in the world, outstripping those held by the 12-nation euro zone and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which stood at a combined $253.6 billion at the end of February. \par \par \uc2  Big gains in Japan's coffers in the past have followed official dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the balance last jumping in October after the ministry bought around $26 billion to keep the yen from strengthening after the September 11 attacks. \par \par \uc2  But no action was taken in the market in the first quarter, even as the yen climbed to a three-month high of 126.36 against the dollar in early March, the ministry said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020509dy59003ee\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
