\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar gains ground, but respite seen brief. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2002\par 09:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 3 (Reuters) - The embattled U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  tallied up some gains in Asian trade on Friday as dollar bears \par \par \uc2  were forced to cover short positions after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market with a half-point rate cut overnight. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded at 127.90 against the yen       ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 90.27 cents against the euro , and 1.6110 against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swiss franc . It had hit a two-month low of 126.96 yen on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But strategists cautioned that any reprieve could be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-lived as the market was second guessing the strength of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. economic recovery, and the dynamism of its asset\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "My discussions with clients and the latest flows data from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. seem to point to a certain reluctance among investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to buy dollar assets," said Karl Broecker, head of treasury at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Landesbank Baden-Wurttemberg in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The monthly average net portfolio inflows to the U.S. in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the first two months of this year were only $12 billion versus\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $43 billion last year. There're doubts about its recovery,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about its corporate sector...bad accounting practice. It's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par clear strong dollar gains are unlikely in the near term," he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading was subdued with Tokyo markets closed for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Constitution Day on Friday and Children's Day on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese markets will resume trading on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SNB TO THE RESCUE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The SNB cut key interest rates on Thursday to counter a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent surge in the Swiss franc due to concerns it might hit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the country's exports and undermine its economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tensions in the Middle East and concerns about labour and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par politics in the euro zone have increased the allure of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traditional safe haven appeal of the Swiss franc.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The move helped pull down the euro, giving the dollar a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par much-needed break after it had languished for weeks against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar was also supported by wariness of potential\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which is known\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to have taken advantage of thin market conditions during\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holidays to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There were rumours that the BOJ was in the market to check\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates, and there was also talk that it had told some banks in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan not to short the dollar," said a dealer at a European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      FOCUS SHIFTED TO EURO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite the yen's recent strength against the dollar -- it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has gained more than four percent since April -- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strategists saw no compelling reason for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to monitor the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par movement of the euro/yen rather than the dollar/yen to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par determine whether to take action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It is still the case of dollar weakness rather than the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen's strength, and that makes it more difficult for the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to go out and buy the dollar," said James\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think the euro/yen is going to be important in terms of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par determining \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the moment. What the BOJ really\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par needs to do is to look for the euro/yen to move down and take\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par advantage of that. But the euro/yen is rather steady now," he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The yen traded at around 115.50 to the euro at 0630\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT which was pretty much within its recent range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Others said a recovery in Japanese asset markets in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past few weeks also removed some of the rationale for the Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at current levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Otherwise, markets will be keeping a close eye on U.S. jobs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data due out later on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. Labor Department is expected to report that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par jobless rate rose in April to 5.8 percent - matching its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highest level in seven years - from 5.7 percent a month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier, according to a Reuters poll of economists.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020503dy5300e1l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
