\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Dollar gains ground, but respite seen brief. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2002\par 08:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 3 (Reuters) - The embattled U.S. dollar tallied up some gains in Asian trade on Friday as dollar bears were forced to cover short positions after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market with a half-point rate cut overnight. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 127.90 against the yen , 90.27 cents against the euro , and 1.6110 against the Swiss franc . It had hit a two-month low of 126.96 yen on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But strategists cautioned that any reprieve could be short-lived as the market was second guessing the strength of the U.S. economic recovery, and the dynamism of its asset markets. \par \par \uc2  "My discussions with clients and the latest flows data from the U.S. seem to point to a certain reluctance among investors to buy dollar assets," said Karl Broecker, head of treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wurttemberg in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The monthly average net portfolio inflows to the U.S. in the first two months of this year were only $12 billion versus $43 billion last year. There're doubts about its recovery, about its corporate sector...bad accounting practice. It's clear strong dollar gains are unlikely in the near term," he said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was subdued with Tokyo markets closed for Constitution Day on Friday and Children's Day on Monday. Japanese markets will resume trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  SNB TO THE RESCUE \par \par \uc2  The SNB cut key interest rates on Thursday to counter a recent surge in the Swiss franc due to concerns it might hit the country's exports and undermine its economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Tensions in the Middle East and concerns about labour and politics in the euro zone have increased the allure of the traditional safe haven appeal of the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  The move helped pull down the euro, giving the dollar a much-needed break after it had languished for weeks against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also supported by wariness of potential dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  which is known to have taken advantage of thin market conditions during holidays to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past. \par \par \uc2  "There were rumours that the BOJ was in the market to check rates, and there was also talk that it had told some banks in Japan not to short the dollar," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  FOCUS SHIFTED TO EURO \par \par \uc2  Despite the yen's recent strength against the dollar - it has gained more than four percent since April - \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists saw no compelling reason for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now. \par \par \uc2  They said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to monitor the movement of the euro/yen rather than the dollar/yen to determine whether to take action. \par \par \uc2  "It is still the case of dollar weakness rather than the yen's strength, and that makes it more difficult for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go out and buy the dollar," said James Malcolm, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "I think the euro/yen is going to be important in terms of determining \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment. What the BOJ really needs to do is to look for the euro/yen to move down and take advantage of that. But the euro/yen is rather steady now," he said. The yen traded at around 115.50 to the euro at 0630 GMT which was pretty much within its recent range. \par \par \uc2  Others said a recovery in Japanese asset markets in the past few weeks also removed some of the rationale for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, markets will be keeping a close eye on U.S. jobs data due out later on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Labor Department is expected to report that the jobless rate rose in April to 5.8 percent - matching its highest level in seven years - from 5.7 percent a month earlier, according to a Reuters poll of economists. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020503dy53007ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
