\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar holds firm tone in U.S. trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2002\par 17:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1624 GMT - Dollar holds a firm tone as firmer U.S. blue chips help market sentiment after overnight gains spurred by Swiss National Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and talk \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unhappy with a stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  - Dow Jones off earlier peaks but still positive, up 10 points, or 0.1 percent. But Nasdaq erases early gains to turn negative. \par \par \uc2  - The dollar gained early against the yen on reports Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  had called securities firms to express its displeasure at the yen's recent gains, raising speculation of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar was trading off the day's low versus the yen around 128 yen , up half a yen on the day and more than 0.30 percent higher. \par \par \uc2  - Traders are waiting to hear from U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill, who will be speaking around noon local time at New York's Asia Society. O'Neill sent the dollar into a tailspin on Wednesday after expressing support for a strong dollar in a way many traders believed lacked conviction. \par \par \uc2  - The dollar rose overnight against the Swiss franc after the Swiss National Bank cut its key short-term interest rate by half a percentage point to dampen the franc's strength. The dollar was off the highs against the franc, hovering just below 1.61 francs , but up 0.40 percent from prior US close. \par \par \uc2  - Euro/dollar back near the day's lows near 90.20 cents as Europe's trading day comes to a close. The ECB left interest rates unchanged, but ECB president Wim Duisenberg said risks to euro zone price stability now were more to the ups