\par\par \b \uc2  Euro/dollar probes session lows near 90 cents. \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2002\par 17:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1501 GMT - Euro/dollar does slow grind to session lows near 90 cents, down 0.30 percent from prior U.S. close. Strong U.S. stock markets, bearish euro zone developments weigh on single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in near term, but losses seen moderated by pessimism over U.S. recovery. \par \par \uc2  - German IG Metall engineering union overwhelmingly votes to strike amid stalled wage negotiations. Though German and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers have in recent days sought to downplay the effects of a strike on the euro zone's largest economy, analysts say it could hamper what is already perceived as a modest recovery. \par \par \uc2  - Meanwhile, French unemployment inches higher, to 9.1 percent in March from 9.0 in previous month. \par \par \uc2  - Consumer Confidence for April comes in at 108.8 from upwardly-revised 110.7 in prior month. Analysts polled by Reuters had expected a 108.0 reading. But present situation and expectations gauges also fell, reflecting consumers' continuing near-term pessimism about the economy. \par \par \uc2  - Chicago Purchasing Managers Index slips to 54.7 in April vs. 55.7 in prior month. Prices paid accelerate to 55.4 versus 51.2 in March. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar/yen gyrates around 128.30 level , off session peaks above 128.50 but above 1-1/2 month lows at 127.65 set a day earlier. Versus yen, euro buys 115.50 yen, off 0.15 percent on the day . \par \par \uc2  - Yen tempered by Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi, who said yen appreciation was inappropriate. However, traders doubtful that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at levels above 125. \par \par \uc2  - Stocks apparently cheer consumer data, after Monday marked longest losing streak in 19 months. Dow Jones Industrial Average adds more than 100 points, Nasdaq Technology average gains 22 points. \par \par \uc2  For full report on major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020430dy4u00uez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
