\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steadies at lows amid US recovery concerns. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Charlotte Cooper \par \uc2 837 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2002\par 14:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 29 (Reuters) - The dollar crumbled further on Monday as worries about a disappointing U.S. recovery and nerves ahead of a key Senate hearing this week drove it down versus the euro, sterling and the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to its weakest level for nearly four months against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and touched a 5-1/2 month low against the franc and the pound. But it managed to struggle back from a 1-1/2 month low against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  Poor U.S. consumer sentiment data on Friday along with the worst week for U.S. equity markets since mid-September dimmed the dollar's attractions and clouded prospects for a strong recovery. "In general the dollar is on the back foot," said David Mann, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. is data is expected to be slightly softer this week, there's a lot of potential for dollar bears to gain pace." \par \par \uc2  By 1215 GMT the dollar was holding just above the session's low of $0.9045 per euro, a level last seen in the wake of January's "europhoria" rally when single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes and coins were introduced. \par \par \uc2  The greenback also dipped to 1.6175 Swiss francs earlier in the European session but struggled back to stand at 1.6200, just a third of a percent down from levels late in New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the pound it broke $1.46 and tested lows not seen since early November. But it staged a comeback from a seven-week low of 127.65 yen set at the tail-end of holiday-thinned Asian trade to stabilise around 128.00. \par \par \uc2  However the greenback fell to its lowest level since December on the FINEX trade-weighted index. \par \par \uc2  DATA WATCH \par \par \uc2  This week's key U.S. data include April consumer confidence figures on Tuesday, the Institute for Supply Management (ISM) survey on Wednesday and labour market data and services sector survey on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts polled by Reuters expect Tuesday's consumer confidence index to fall to 107.0 in April from 110.2 in March. \par \par \uc2  The ISM index (formerly NAPM) is forecast to dip to 55.4 in April from 55.6. The jobs data is seen a little better in comparison, with the unemployment rate expected to remain unchanged at 5.7 percent in April. \par \par \uc2  "This week's data will hardly support the dollar," said Armin Mekelburg, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich. \par \par \uc2  But traders and analysts said the key focus was a U.S. Senate Banking Committee hearing on Wednesday when Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill, defender of the U.S. strong dollar policy, will brief the committee about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  The hearing includes Jerry Jasinowski, president of the National Association of Manufacturers, and other industry representatives irritated at the dollar's strength. \par \par \uc2  "People are positioning ahead of O'Neill's testimony on Wednesday and on concerns over the size of the U.S. current account deficit," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's decline should moderate in coming days as short-term players, who have driven a lot of the action, will eventually take profits." \par \par \uc2  EURO CAUTION \par \par \uc2  Adding to caution over the potential for dollar losses this week was data showing that the short-term speculative market was holding its biggest ever net long position in euros in the week ending April 23, making it potentially hard for the euro to move much higher from here. \par \par \uc2  The focus for monetary policy is on the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's council meeting on Thursday. Analysts expect the ECB to leave rates unchanged at 3.25 percent with recent euro zone data showing inflation falling against a backdrop of moderate growth. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank president and ECB board member Ernst Welteke said on Monday he still expected euro zone inflation to fall below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2.0 percent target ceiling this year but recognised it may not happen in the first half. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone current account data showed net portfolio and foreign direct investment outflow of 19.8 billion euros in February, slowing from 36.9 billion in January. \par \par \uc2  "If we are seeing a sustainable turnaround in the euro, this should start showing up in the portfolio flow data for March and particularly April," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  TOKYO HOLIDAY \par \par \uc2  Japan was closed for the Green Day holiday making Asian trading thin. Dealers said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was backed by strong performance of Japanese equities in recent sessions, compared with Wall Street where profit worries have kept stocks depressed. \par \par \uc2  But the Japanese monetary authorities are likely to step up their verbal campaign against a stronger yen although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still more than 10 yen off the level \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb export-damaging yen strength. \par \par \uc2  "If the dollar/yen goes below 120 the chance of outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is high," Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020429dy4t00pxo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
