\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen inches lower, Japan injects caution. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2002\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 24 (Reuters) - The yen edged further away from recent one-month highs against the dollar on Wednesday as Japanese policy-makers resumed their complaints about a stronger Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Worries that U.S. assets have little more to gain from prospects of a global recovery have weighed on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  But after going quiet early in the week, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  rediscovered its voice late on Tuesday when its head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Haruhiko Kuroda, told journalists in New York that the yen should not appreciate against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  He was backed up on Wednesday by senior MOF official Zembei Mizoguchi who argued that there were no new factors to prompt the yen to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese officials appear to be relatively comfortable with the dollar in a 130-135 yen range," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "Every time the dollar gets anywhere near 130, you can expect verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to two-day highs of 130.44 yen and was trading at 130.31/36 at 0715 GMT, up 0.10 percent from the New York close and nearly one yen stronger than one-month lows set last week. \par \par \uc2  The euro was steady against the dollar at $0.8881/85, from one-week lows around $0.8850 set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  German producer prices rose 0.3 percent month-on-month in March, a smaller rise than expected but still reflecting the recent sharp rise in oil prices. \par \par \uc2  The European Union releases its semi-annual economic forecasts at 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  While there was talk that potential regional strikes by Germany's powerful IG Metall union and the shock success of far-right nationalist Jean-Marie Le Pen in France should be negative for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro has proved resilient in recent days. \par \par \uc2  One or more of the euro-zone national central banks was said to be buying euros, apparently for commercial purposes, around $0.8850. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite bizarre the way the euro's been holding up given all the negative news out of Europe," said Marshall Gittler, head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "I have to assume people really are uncertain about the U.S. recovery and whether it can keep attracting enough offshore money to fund its current account deficit," he added. \par \par \uc2  The deficit has long been shrugged off by U.S. officials and largely ignored by markets, but now that it is steadily nearing five percent of gross domestic product, more doomsayers are appearing in print. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Nobel Prize-winning economist Robert Mundell said the deficit was driving the nation deeper into the debt of foreign creditors and could undermine the strength of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  CHANGE OF TACK \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sudden reversion to verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  left traders exasperated since only a day ago Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa had insisted that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels should be determined by markets. \par \par \uc2  "When they say \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the market, what they mean is, 'left to the market as long as the market does what we want it to do'," said Bank of America's Gittler. \par \par \uc2  Japanese economic indicators on Wednesday confirmed a patchy recovery, in contrast to a firmer upswing in global conditions. \par \par \uc2  The government said its all-industries index rose 0.5 percent in February from the previous month. But the core tertiary sector component, mainly comprising service industries, fell 0.4 percent for a third straight month of declines. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers were hoping that U.S. durable goods orders and the Federal Reserve's Beige Book due out later on Wednesday might give them something to trade on. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan made it clear last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had doubts about the pace of recovery and was in no rush to raise interest rates, thus greatly limiting the potential impact of any single piece of data. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020424dy4o00flz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
