\par\par \b \uc2  Yen on defensive as Japan authorities stay vocal. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 13 (Reuters) - The yen inched down on Wednesday, on the defensive after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry kept alive the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reverse its recent rise. \par \par \uc2  But with the yen drawing sizeable demand from Japanese exporters and some U.S. names, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were kept in a tight range in subdued trade. \par \par \uc2  The market was pepped up early when Japan's Jiji news agency quoted a U.S. auto industry group leader expressing concern about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities "just because there was a rebalancing of three to four yen". \par \par \uc2  While that helped sentiment for the yen, the report was soon countered by a reminder from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat remained intact. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said he continued to watch \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves closely, adding it was important for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move in a stable manner. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have been vocal in recent sessions after the yen soared almost five yen in one week to hit a near three-month high of 126.36 yen per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The firmer yen has fuelled a positive mood in Japanese stock and bond markets, but could hurt Japan's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The ministry's well-worn line surprised no one, but kept the dollar supported. The greenback drifted near the firmer end of its morning range by midday at 129.21/26 yen after an earlier dip to 128.95. \par \par \uc2  "Mizoguchi's remarks today weren't very strong, but the fact that officials are coming out with comments on a daily basis should keep the dollar well-bid," said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The yen was also restrained against the euro, with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 112.98/113.09 yen from around 112.00 yen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  EYES ON STOCKS \par \par \uc2  Traders also looked to Tokyo stocks for direction, though they got little inspiration as an early one percent rise in the benchmark Nikkei average lost steam. \par \par \uc2  "There may be some scepticism whether the Nikkei can sustain recent gains beyond the fiscal year-end," said Masayuki Yamamoto, research analyst at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "Much of the rise has been due to technical factors so stocks look vulnerable when Japan's fundamentals problems like deflation and banks' bad debt remain unresolved," he said. \par \par \uc2  But traders said that fragility in sentiment could also see last-minute fund repatriation by Japanese investors before the end of the business year, proving supportive for the yen. \par \par \uc2  Capital flows data on Wednesday showed Japanese investors had sold a hefty net 673.6 billion yen ($5.21 billion) of foreign securities in February, a seasonal move seen aimed at dressing up finances before book-closings. \par \par \uc2  They had sold a much heavier net 3.3572 trillion yen of foreign securities in January. \par \par \uc2  EURO WEATHERS GDP \par \par \uc2  The euro struggled to rise, but showed muted reaction to news overnight that eurozone gross domestic product suffered its first quarter-on-quarter drop in nearly a decade. \par \par \uc2  The euro held at $0.8747/57 in thin trading from $0.8753 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  The market looked to U.S. February retail sales and a speech by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan later in the day for the latest read on the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  Retail sales figures are expected to come in strong, with a Reuters poll estimating a rise of 0.9 percent in February after a 0.2 percent drop in the previous month. ($1=129.17 Yen). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0317 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 12 Mar.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.8745   0.8755   -0.11    -1.79   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen               129.19   128.92   +0.21    -1.85   131.63\par  Euro/yen              113.00   112.88   +0.11    -3.62   117.24\par  Dlr/swiss             1.6795   1.6773   +0.13    +1.21   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr               1.4141   1.4148   -0.05    -2.75   1.4541\par  Can/dlr               1.5872   1.5850   +0.14    -0.28   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr               0.5197   0.5203   -0.12    +1.78   0.5106\par  Euro/swiss            1.4692   1.4684   +0.05    -0.60   1.4780\par  Euro/stg              0.6182   0.6182   +0.00    +0.96   0.6123.\par \par \par \par     For full report on major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ..        Debt...      Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \pa