\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Govt Warnings Show Preference For Dlr Above Y130 \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jamie McGeever \par \uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 15:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    LONDON -(Dow Jones)- Japanese government pension fund allocations may\par be helping push the yen lower Tuesday, but it's what authorities are\par saying on exchange rates that's exerting greater influence over the\par Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other government officials are speaking out more and more on exchange rate moves following the yen's rapid gains against the dollar last week. \par \par \uc2  Their increasingly vocal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a clear sign they'd prefer to see the dollar back above Y130.00 and, in all likelihood, quite a bit higher, observers say. \par \par \uc2  To this end, they'd have been quietly satisfied at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's reaction to the new Government Pension Investment Fund allocations. \par \par \uc2  Of the GPIF's extra Y9 trillion earmarked for investments in the 2002 fiscal year, Y3 trillion, or 33%, will be channeled into foreign bonds and stocks. Analysts had expected no more than 20% of the extra money to go overseas. \par \par \uc2  Dealers immediately pushed the dollar up to within a whisker of Y129.00, although it has since eased back to around Y128.75. \par \par \uc2  At 1430 GMT Tuesday, the dollar was at Y128.78, while the Nikkei closed 2.6% down at 11607.33. \par \par \uc2  But the extra GPIF outflows will only weaken the yen on the margins, given that the investments will be spread out over the course of the whole fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  What's bound to have a much harder impact, however, is verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There's been a lot of it in recent days, and there's likely to be a lot more. \par \par \uc2  "Comments from Japanese officials (show that) they want dollar/yen above Y130.00," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "They're uncomfortable with current (exchange rate) prices," agreed Mark Austin, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC in London. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                Verbal, Not Actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It's the Y130.00 level that many regard as the pivotal point in this\par cross.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late last year, when the dollar was making its way up toward Y130.00,\par Japanese officials said the greenback still had room to strengthen. When\par it pushed through Y130.00, there were no complaints.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even the dollar's recent slide, sparked by U.S. hedge fund liquidation\par of long dollar positions, didn't draw any comment from Tokyo until\par Y130.00 support broke last Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since then, however, not a day's gone by without at least two\par high-ranking government officials on the wires warning against "rapid"\par or "abrupt" moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The threat of actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around current levels, however,\par remains a distant one. Not once in 206 official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par last 12 years has the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought dollars above Y120.50,\par according to Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even a fall below Y125.00, which would certainly turn up the volume\par and intensity of verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , probably wouldn't trigger actual\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Especially with the Nikkei stock market above 11,000\par points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And the verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might remove the need for actual\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in any case, point out analysts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jamie McGeever, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 207 842 9483;\par jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020312dy3c000wh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
