\par\par \b \uc2  IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  mixed, yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears wane. \b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 16:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Reuters is considering eliminating this opening report and sending one market report per day on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures timed as soon as possible after the close of the IMM. We welcome your comments. Please e-mail greg.mccune@reuters.com) \par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, March 11 (Reuters) - IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures were mixed in early U.S. dealings on Monday with June yen marginally higher after support from a thinly-veiled \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat evaporated. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  international bureau, said Japan was ready to take steps if the rapid yen gains seen last week resume. The yen contract ramped up to $0.007995, its highest level since Dec. 13, last week partly on hefty gains in Japanese stocks. \par \par \uc2  "The initial response was to heighten fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and put a little pressure on the yen," said Michael Malpede, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco. "But you still have the stronger repatriation flows. I think that's all leading toward a little bit of support for the yen." \par \par \uc2  Some traders linked recent yen strength in part to yen repatriation flows ahead of the Japanese fiscal year end on March 31. \par \par \uc2  Floor traders, however, were preoccupied with spread trading - the shift from March futures contracts to June contracts. June contracts replaced March as the lead month on Monday. \par \par \uc2  June yen sat in positive territory in Friday's range, which in turn was lodged in Thursday's enormous range of $0.007682 to $0.007955. \par \par \uc2  One trader said yen futures were a little higher on weaker U.S. equities. June Standard & Poor 500 futures index were lower in Friday's range. June Nasdaq composite index futures also were lower in Friday's range. \par \par \uc2  "I still don't think the dollar trend has changed," he said. "Stocks are getting hit so that's a little bit negative." \par \par \uc2  Resistance for yen futures was at $0.007898, Friday's high, ahead of the the 100-day moving average at $0.007883, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  June euros also were slightly higher and stuck in Friday's range of $0.8687 to $0.8800. Malpede said dollar weakness versus the euro was the result of an interview with U.S. Commerce Undersecretary Grant Aldonas in the Financial Times. The newspaper quoted Aldonas as saying Washington could level tariffs on imports from other sectors besides steel unless Europe and Japan reflate their economies. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the Bush administration put tariffs on imported steel, which has cheapened relative to U.S.-produced steel as the dollar strengthens against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The action called into question the U.S. commitment to a strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I think the trade situation is weighing on the dollar/euro," Malpede said. \par \par \uc2  Resistance for June euros was at Friday's high of $0.8800, technical analysts said. \par \par \uc2  At 9:21 a.m CST (1521 GMT), June yen were up $0.000026 at $0.007842, euros were up $0.0018 at $0.8720, Swiss francs rose $0.0025 to $0.5953, sterling rose $0.0006 to $1.4132, Canadian dollars rose 0.0005 to at $0.6308, Aussie dollars fell $0.0020 to $0.5178 and Mexican pesos rose $0.000150 to $0.108600. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020311dy3b00uw5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picw