\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Kuroda Shows Japan Satisfied With Yen's Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2002\par 05:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japan, which welcomed the yen's slide since late last year, is now signaling it's satisfied and that it wants its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stable recently," top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda said Monday, using \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -policy code to signify the Finance Ministry isn't pushing for a further yen drop. \par \par \uc2  That's a clear departure for Kuroda, vice minister for international affairs, and his deputy, Zembei Mizoguchi, who until the past few days were saying the yen was still correcting from previously excessive strength. \par \par \uc2  When the dollar was sinking last year, Japan was clearly alarmed that a strong yen would deepen recession and worsen already harsh deflation. \par \par \uc2  The authorities sold a record Y3.2 trillion for dollars and euros in September, helping hoist the dollar up from that month's low of Y115.80. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under orders from the ministry, stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the dollar hit about Y120, but Kuroda and Mizoguchi continued actively talking the yen down well into this year. \par \par \uc2  Recently, as South Korea and China began to complain that the weak yen was hurting their export competitiveness and the U.S. warned Tokyo not to "manipulate" its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to seek an export-led recovery, Japanese officials increasingly stressed that the yen's fall merely reflected Japan's weak fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The greenback hit Y135.19 on Jan. 31, its highest since late 1998. Around 0425 GMT Monday, the dollar was trading at Y133.80. \par \par \uc2  That seems to be far enough for now. \par \par \uc2  Amplifying on Kuroda's remarks, one of his predecessors as vice minister, Toyoo Gyohten, said, "A weaker yen will not benefit Japanese industries." \par \par \uc2  In an interview in Monday's Nihon Keizai Shimbun, Gyohten said the dollar's appropriate range may be Y110-Y130. \par \par \uc2  "For the stability of the Japanese economy, it will be important that the dollar/yen rate stay near that range for the near term," Gyohten said, adding that a dollar rise "to Y140-Y150 would bring about problems." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda and Gyohten both urged the BOJ to ease monetary policy further, in line with Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa's call for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase its purchases of Japanese government bonds by 25% to Y1 trillion a month at Thursday's monetary policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  If the BOJ complies, however, that could increase downward pressure on the yen. \par \par \uc2  While Japan's money supply, as measured by M2+CDs, rose just 3.6% in January from a year earlier, monetary base - \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in circulation plus banks' reserves at the BOJ - soared 23% on-year in January, the fastest expansion since 1974. \par \par \uc2  This jump, two-and-a-half times the speed of U.S. monetary-base expansion thanks to the BOJ's "quantitative easing," suggesting further yen weakness as the supply of yen mushrooms compared to that of dollars, The Economist magazine said in its most recent issue. \par \par \uc2  Citing Lehman Brothers data showing a high correlation between relative monetary-base growth and the dollar/yen rate over the past decade, the magazine implied a further yen fall ahead, which could test Japan's tolerance for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -Tokyo Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020225dy2p0007e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
