\par\par \b \uc2  FORUM-France's Fabius rules out target ranges for euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2002\par 19:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Feb 2 (Reuters) - French Finance Minister Laurent Fabius on Saturday ruled out the idea of setting informal floor and ceiling targets for the euro-dollar exchange rate to be defended by the U.S. and European central banks. \par \par \uc2  "If you think about the euro against the dollar, it's decided on by the markets, and it's fair," Fabius told Reuters, when questioned about a suggestion made at a World Economic Forum session that the Group of Seven industrialised nations set and defend a target exchange rate range to avoid excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability. \par \par \uc2  Central banks should manage their own monetary policy properly and leave the markets to determine exchange rates, Fabius said. \par \par \uc2  Nobel Prize-winning economist Robert Mundell, an expert on monetary union, said a table of businessmen and policymakers he led proposed the next G7 finance ministers' meeting should set a de facto floor of about 85 cents to the euro and a ceiling of about $1.15 to limit damaging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve Board, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Britain and Canada \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly in September 2000 to support the euro after it fell to 84.40 cents from a January 1999 launch value of $1.17. \par \par \uc2  Fabius brushed aside concerns about the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current exchange rate of 86 cents, saying it was better to not focus on short-term fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously, some people say it's weakening if we compare it to the U.S. dollar, but you have not to pay too much attention to a situation of one month or two months. I think it will be a success because it's a worldwide \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Fabius declined to say whether European Union finance ministers would endorse on Feb. 12 a recommendation by the European Commission, the EU's executive body, to warn Germany because its budget deficit is nearing an EU limit of 3 percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  But he said: "I think the stability agreement is a very important element and all of us - France, Germany, Spain and different countries - agree on that. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's part of the rules of the club and you must not change that." \par \par \uc2  He said he was confident the German economy would recover because the German government was "a serious government". \par \par \uc2  Fabius said he expected Britain to decide, maybe in 2003, to join the euro because it would want to be one of the "ins" making key decisions rather than one of the historical "outs". \par \par \uc2  "(Prime Minister) Tony Blair is in favour of the euro and I think if people share the view of Tony Blair, it will good for Great Britain and for the rest of the euro," he said. \par \par \uc2  EU finance ministry officials discussed on Friday whether to formally warn Germany over its burgeoning budget deficit but failed to reach agreement, sources said. \par \par \uc2  "It was a totally inconclusive meeting. My reading is that there will be a reprimand for Germany but not in the form that the Commission is expecting," one source said. \par \par \uc2  The Commission sparked controversy by proposing on Wednesday to issue an "early warning" to Berlin. \par \par \uc2  Germany's deficit was 2.6 percent of GDP in 2001 and is forecast by the EU executive to hit 2.7 percent this year. Under the bloc's Stability and Growth Pact, which Germany designed, governments can be fined if deficits exceed 3.0 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020202dy2200qjq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
