\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Mizoguchi:Policy Of Taking Proper  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Steps Unchanged \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2001\par 01:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Japanese government's policy of taking appropriate steps in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prevent the yen from rising too much against the dollar and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unchanged, a senior MOF official said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Our stance of taking proper measures (against a yen rise) remains unchanged," Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the international bureau at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said when asked about the dollar's overnight fall to as low as Y122.62 from the low Y123's. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi reiterated that the ministry continues to watch the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closely. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi said a strong yen doesn't reflect the weak fundamentals of Japan's economy at this time. \par \par \uc2  "This isn't a situation for the yen to be strong. The yen should reflect (weak) economic fundamentals," Mizoguchi said. "A yen rise is undesirable." \par \par \uc2  To curb the yen's rise, the finance ministry conducted massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars and euros in late September, following the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks in the U.S. that led to a sharp fall in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0115 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y122.71, just up from Y122.62 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2942;\par ron.harui@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011121dxbl0001o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
