\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Firm But Gains Capped As Direction Sought \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miyako Takebe \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2001\par 07:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar remained firmly supported against the yen in Asia Wednesday, though it failed to extend gains as players paused to consider whether it was safe to keep backing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While the dollar managed to hold on to its gains logged overnight on reports of military gains in Afghanistan, it was unable to chase higher ground as the market pondered the future direction of the greenback now that recent short-covering has run its course, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market's not sure whether it should close its eyes to short-term negatives coming out of the U.S. and keep betting on a stronger dollar in the belief a sooner-than-expected U.S. recovery may be possible if there is an early conclusion in Afghanistan,"," said Minoru Shioiri, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Kokusai Securities. \par \par \uc2  But with players unable to make a clear decision Wednesday, the uncertainty and offers from Japanese investors dragged the dollar off its intraday high of Y121.80 and kept it hovering around Y121.50 for most of the Asian session, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Even though Kabul has been captured, there is still likely to be confusion surrounding the establishment of a new Afghan government to replace the Taliban, and its uncertain for how long dollar buying will continue," said Satoshi Tate, vice president at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  What is clear, however, is the market's dislike of the euro, which continued to remained weak after falling to three-month lows below $0.8800 overnight. \par \par \uc2  In addition to the market's lack of faith in the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to support the Euro-zone economies, supply-demand factors such as lingering capital outflows related to the reweighting of the Morgan Stanley Capital International, or MSCI, indexes, continue to weigh on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Its easier now to sell the euro than it is to actively buy the dollar, which is why the dollar is finding it harder to rise against the yen than the euro," said Kokusai's Shioiri. \par \par \uc2  "If there were a catalyst which would allow the yen to be hammered in the same way, the dollar would probably rise," he said, adding none of the current yen-bearish factors are likely to cause such selling. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y121.55, below Y121.61 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y120.91 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.8824, higher than $0.8810 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $0.8914 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y107.26, down from Y107.14 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y107.78 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  For the near term, stability in U.S. share prices and hopes of a U.S. recovery will likely underpin the dollar, although it may not be enough to give the market a clear direction, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities' well-known vigilance against a stronger yen will also likely continue to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above Y120.00, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi repeated Wednesday that there is no change to Japan's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Tokyo has maintained a strong yen wouldn't reflect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weak economic fundamentals, and authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen when its rise has been viewed as too excessive. \par \par \uc2  While the market looks for new direction, "extremely low volatilities on one-month dollar/yen options, which are currently in the 8% levels, will likely make it easier for profit-taking to emerge on minor gains," Sanwa's Tate said. \par \par \uc2  Volatilities on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options gauge the anticipated moves in the underlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with low volatility implying a narrower trading range. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sterling was at $1.4425, down slightly from $1.4430 in New York and\par lower than $1.4520 in Tokyo Tuesday.\par   -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates which accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture which is updated\par hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par -0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011114dxbe000d4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adju